    <string name="aboutScreen_airGappedTitle" formatted="false">Air-gapped sovereign AI</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_airGappedBody" formatted="false">BoarLite is an offline-first mobile AI system exploring adaptive model routing, local retrieval, and resource-aware inference. It performs local LLM inference via llama.rn / llama.cpp and local hybrid retrieval (SQLite FTS5 + on-device embeddings) with zero cloud dependencies.</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_hardwareTitle" formatted="false">Hardware architecture &amp; budget</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_hardwareBody" formatted="false">Complies with strict mobile field constraints: resident memory remains capped under 12GB RAM using memory-mapped weights (mmap), and total storage is audited against a 50GB storage envelope.</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_benchmarkTitle" formatted="false">Benchmark it yourself</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_benchmarkBody" formatted="false">BoarLite measures every answer on your own phone: model load time, time to first token, tokens/sec, peak memory and which sources were used. Run the built-in evaluation from Execution Telemetry → 🧪 Evaluate to compare any installed model on the same questions, or run it from a computer over adb (see AGENTS.md on GitHub).</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_repoTitle" formatted="false">Open source repository</string>
    <string name="aboutScreen_repoBody" formatted="false">Source code, quantized model manifests, and offline indexing scripts are available at:</string>
